# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Normalize line endings in the repository.
#
# WHY: a contributor with `core.autocrlf=false` (Linux/macOS default, or a
# Windows git installed with the wrong option) would otherwise commit CRLF and
# silently turn the "pure format" style commit into a full-file line-ending
# flip — invisible in `--shortstat`, invisible in review. Forcing LF on
# checkout makes ruff (line-ending="auto") follow the worktree automatically,
# so the format gate never goes permanently red on Windows either.
#
# ruff.toml intentionally keeps line-ending="auto" (NOT forced to "lf"): with
# autocrlf=true a forced "lf" would fight the CRLF checkout and
# `ruff format --check` would fail on every file. .gitattributes is the correct
# lever. (SRE/code-review decision; see .pre-commit-config.yaml.)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
* text=auto
*.py text eol=lf
